# {{.ProviderName}} Provider

{{.Description}}

OmniDDI is CheckRed's DNS, DHCP and IP address management (DDI) platform. The provider manages DNS zones and records, IPAM containers and subnets, and DHCP subnets and host reservations through the OmniDDI management server. Views, network spaces, IPAM nodes and server groups are read through data sources.

## Authentication

The provider signs in with the `username` and `password` of an OmniDDI account and works with that account's roles. Use a dedicated automation account without MFA, and pass the password through `OMNIDDI_PASSWORD`. Set `network_space_id` to work in a network space other than the account's landing space. See the [authentication guide](guides/authentication) for the recommended account setup.

## Environment variables

Every attribute can be set from the environment. The attribute wins when both are present.

| Attribute | Environment variable |
|---|---|
| `endpoint` | `OMNIDDI_ENDPOINT` |
| `username` | `OMNIDDI_USERNAME` |
| `password` | `OMNIDDI_PASSWORD` |
| `network_space_id` | `OMNIDDI_NETWORK_SPACE_ID` |
| `ca_cert_pem` | `OMNIDDI_CA_CERT_PEM` |
| `client_cert_pem` | `OMNIDDI_CLIENT_CERT_PEM` |
| `client_key_pem` | `OMNIDDI_CLIENT_KEY_PEM` |
| `proxy_url` | `OMNIDDI_PROXY_URL` |
| `insecure` | `OMNIDDI_INSECURE` |
| `timeout` | `OMNIDDI_TIMEOUT` |
| `approval_mode` | `OMNIDDI_APPROVAL_MODE` |
| `max_concurrency` | `OMNIDDI_MAX_CONCURRENCY` |
| `max_retries` | `OMNIDDI_MAX_RETRIES` |

## TLS, proxy and mutual TLS

- `ca_cert_pem` adds a private CA to the trusted roots.
- `client_cert_pem` and `client_key_pem` enable mutual TLS and must be set together.
- `proxy_url` sets an HTTP proxy. When it is unset, the standard `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` variables are honored.
- `insecure = true` skips certificate verification and prints a warning on every run. Use it for development only.

